# path: /v1/chat/completions
# base-url: https://api.meta.ai   (export META_BASE_URL=https://api.meta.ai ; the path above carries /v1)
# content-type: json
# model: muse-spark-1.3-contributor   (user decision 2026-10-28: contributor tier, training on our prompts is acceptable, cheaper)
# input: the character cutout image (PNG/JPEG, <= 512 px long side as the pipeline sends it) -> {{INPUT_MIME}}/{{INPUT_B64}}
# changed 2026-10-28 (T07): the sheet is written by Spark vision LOOKING at the character: one text part + one
#   image_url part, like spark-score. The text is Prompts.characterSheet("", withImage = true) verbatim; when the app
#   has a description it becomes "The image shows a character a child drew: <description>. Reply ...". Without an
#   image MetaApi still sends the old plain-string message ("A child drew a character: <description>. Reply ...").
#   The drawing-01 sheet fixture was probed with the old text-only shape (input drawing-01.description.txt).
# verified: https://dev.meta.ai/docs/features/structured-output + https://dev.meta.ai/docs/features/chat-completion (2026-10-28):
#   response_format {"type":"json_schema","json_schema":{"name","schema"}} is supported on Chat Completions and the
#   JSON string lands in choices[0].message.content. Use strict:true + additionalProperties:false.
# unverified: Kazakh output quality of Muse Spark 1.3 (no language list in the docs); the Day 1 probe decides.
# unverified: whether "strict": true rejects the nested "lines" object; drop strict if the call returns 400.
# changed 2026-11-03: "name" became "names" {kk, ru, en} and "lines" gained "en", so the app shows the name and the
#   lines in the chosen language. Fixtures recorded before that have one "name" (SheetParser keeps it as the Kazakh name)
#   and no "en" lines (SheetParser pads them with its generic English lines).
# probed 2026-10-28: max_completion_tokens 600 returned finish_reason "length" with content null (reasoning tokens
#   count against the budget) -> raised to 2048 and reasoning_effort "low" (mirrors core/meta Prompts).
# changed 2026-11-11 (T40): the sheet also carries the duel stats: "stats" {power, speed, guard, agility} raw 1-10
#   (StatBudget.normalise rebalances them to 20 points), "why" {kk, ru, en} -> {power, speed, guard, agility} reasons of
#   at most 4 words, "view" front|side|back, "faces" left|right. All four are required in the strict schema and optional
#   for SheetParser (sheets recorded before have none and fight with their ability's archetype).
#   max_completion_tokens 2048 -> 3072: the visible reply roughly doubles (~500 tokens) and judging the picture adds
#   reasoning. Unprobed with stats until the live re-record.
{
  "model": "muse-spark-1.3-contributor",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": [
        { "type": "text", "text": "The image shows a character a child drew. Reply with JSON only: {\"names\": {\"kk\": a short friendly name in Kazakh (Cyrillic script), \"ru\": the same name in Russian, \"en\": the same name in English}, \"personality\": one sentence, \"ability\": one of \"jump\",\"fly\",\"roll\",\"hide\", \"lines\": {\"kk\": [5 short lines in Kazakh the character says], \"ru\": [the same 5 lines in Russian], \"en\": [the same 5 lines in English]}, \"stats\": {\"power\": 1 to 10, \"speed\": 1 to 10, \"guard\": 1 to 10, \"agility\": 1 to 10}, \"why\": {\"kk\": {\"power\": reason, \"speed\": reason, \"guard\": reason, \"agility\": reason} in Kazakh, \"ru\": the same reasons in Russian, \"en\": the same reasons in English}, \"view\": one of \"front\",\"side\",\"back\", \"faces\": one of \"left\",\"right\"}. Lines are for a child, max 6 words each. Score the stats from what is visible on the character, never from its name: claws, horns or a big body give power; wings, wheels or long legs give speed; a shell, armour or a thick body give guard; a small light body, a tail or many legs give agility. The scores are rebalanced afterwards so every character gets the same total: spreading them matters more than their size, so score high what the character clearly has and low what it lacks. Each reason names what you see, at most 4 words, for a child. \"view\" is which side of the character the picture shows (front: it looks at us, side: a profile, back: it looks away); \"faces\" is where a side view looks in the picture, and only matters for a side view." },
        { "type": "image_url", "image_url": { "url": "data:{{INPUT_MIME}};base64,{{INPUT_B64}}" } }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "response_format": {
    "type": "json_schema",
    "json_schema": {
      "name": "CharacterSheet",
      "strict": true,
      "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "names": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "kk": { "type": "string" },
              "ru": { "type": "string" },
              "en": { "type": "string" }
            },
            "required": ["kk", "ru", "en"]
          },
          "personality": { "type": "string" },
          "ability": { "type": "string", "enum": ["jump", "fly", "roll", "hide"] },
          "lines": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "kk": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } },
              "ru": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } },
              "en": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } }
            },
            "required": ["kk", "ru", "en"]
          },
          "stats": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "power": { "type": "integer" },
              "speed": { "type": "integer" },
              "guard": { "type": "integer" },
              "agility": { "type": "integer" }
            },
            "required": ["power", "speed", "guard", "agility"]
          },
          "why": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "kk": {
                "type": "object",
                "additionalProperties": false,
                "properties": {
                  "power": { "type": "string" },
                  "speed": { "type": "string" },
                  "guard": { "type": "string" },
                  "agility": { "type": "string" }
                },
                "required": ["power", "speed", "guard", "agility"]
              },
              "ru": {
                "type": "object",
                "additionalProperties": false,
                "properties": {
                  "power": { "type": "string" },
                  "speed": { "type": "string" },
                  "guard": { "type": "string" },
                  "agility": { "type": "string" }
                },
                "required": ["power", "speed", "guard", "agility"]
              },
              "en": {
                "type": "object",
                "additionalProperties": false,
                "properties": {
                  "power": { "type": "string" },
                  "speed": { "type": "string" },
                  "guard": { "type": "string" },
                  "agility": { "type": "string" }
                },
                "required": ["power", "speed", "guard", "agility"]
              }
            },
            "required": ["kk", "ru", "en"]
          },
          "view": { "type": "string", "enum": ["front", "side", "back"] },
          "faces": { "type": "string", "enum": ["left", "right"] }
        },
        "required": ["names", "personality", "ability", "lines", "stats", "why", "view", "faces"]
      }
    }
  },
  "reasoning_effort": "low",
  "max_completion_tokens": 3072
}
